  "rationale": "The five contract fixtures pin the five acceptance criteria. SearchUsesTheMarketplaceImplementationTests proves a run selects the url builder and parser for the marketplace the work carries, not the first registration. NonPaginatingMarketplaceSearchTests proves a non-paginating marketplace is fetched once whatever MaxPages says while a paginating one still walks every configured page. ResultCardsWithoutListingsFailRunPerMarketplaceTests proves, per marketplace, that a markup-bearing page parsing to zero listings fails the run and a genuinely empty page completes it. EbaySearchParityThroughMarketplaceSelectionTests and EbayItemPageParserServiceTests prove eBay's url shape and parse results survive the selection split. RefreshActsOnSubstitutedItemPageParseTests proves the refresh path uses an injected item-page parser and acts on its result. The shape files declare the marketplace identity on the search interfaces, the SupportsPagination capability, the parser-owned markup predicate, the IItemPageParser seam and the throwing stubs that make the command red until the implementer lands the behaviour; a scratch implementation of only those bodies turned the full Unit (103) and Architecture (25) suites green.",
